# Fichero Release Notes

## 0.0.6 – JULY 1, 2025
- Added settings for Plans, Projects, and Prompts. 
- Major refactor of Director.py
- Wrote backend to run on Python, and not require REDIS and Celery.
- Rewrote plans format, to not rely on Weasel.
- Removed Weasel backend.
- Tested on 50 folders, consiting on 7992 images.
- Added rembg (AI background removal), which is now optional. If not available, the app falls back to contour-based background removal. The GUI disables the AI background removal option if rembg is not present on Mac. This ensures  compatibility for ARM Macs and other platforms where rembg/scikit-image is problematic.
- Made ultralytics optional in crop.py so we can build for mac. 
  - Added YOLO_AVAILABLE flag to check if YOLO is available
  - Added fallback to contour-based cropping when YOLO is not available
  - Updated crop_with_yolo() to return None if YOLO not available
  - Updated crop_batch() to handle YOLO loading failures gracefully

- To Do:
    - Remove library for settings window.
    - Update activity monmitor window
    - Hook up or remove all GUI elements.
    - Build and run. 
    - Add in PDF export. 

## 0.0.5 – JUNE 15, 2025
- Added menus.
- Added user interface translation support.
- Added an About window, inspireed by BBedit.
- Created settings window, that lets you edit API Keys for Open AI and Qwen.
    - Added app settings for API Keys. API Keys are loaded from environment variables if available; otherwise, they can be set via the Settings window. API Keys are saved, encrypted, in the appropriate folder based on the operating system.

## 0.0.4 – JUNE 13, 2025
- Added Briefcase for easier packaging and  distributing of Fichero.
- Integrated Toga for macOS/Windows/Linux GUI development. GUI is inspired, for now, by John Siracusa's [Hyperspace](https://hypercritical.co/2025/02/25/hyperspace).
- Refactored the project structure by moving files into the `src` directory, needed for Toga and Brieface. 
- Refactored code to work with the structure.

## 0.0.3 – JUNE 5, 2025
- Added support for multi-step LLM processing, using llm_process.py, llm_utils.py, and a config file. Tested with OpenAI models. Config files set prompts, choose batch sizes, decide between sending pages individually or in groups up to chunk size based on max tokens, allow combining results, and sending previous results. ,
- Added a config file to auto-catalogue by generating using LLMs named entity recognition for people, places, organizations, events, but also specific things we are interested in, e.g. mines, animals, plants, injuries; a timeline of events; most important people; ten tags or keywords; and a 150 word summary.

## 0.0.2 – MAY 25, 2025
- Added support for running on multiple processors and in parallel, and doing asynchronous transcription calls. Fichero_director.py.

## 0.0.1 – MAY 9, 2025
- Initial development release, which crops, splits, rotates, enhances, removes background, and transcribes.